Assume that \((DP)\) and \((DD)\) satisfy the regularity condition. Then exactly one of the following holds:
\[
\begin{aligned}
&\text{(i) Both problems are feasible, each has an optimal solution, and }z_0=w_0;\\
&\text{(ii) One problem is infeasible, and the other is either infeasible or has no finite optimum.}
\end{aligned}
\]
